  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set version = \"4.2.3\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: qgis\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://qgis.org/downloads/qgis-{{ version }}.tar.bz2\n  sha256: b044889d895c07d9355512cba76973822830153f6f15feb0d5e00077d3d76e59\n  patches:\n    - 0001-fix-protobuf-23.patch\n    - 0002-skip-dot-in-path.patch  # [win]\n    - 0005-check-locks-not-destroyed.patch\n    - 0006-use-entrypoints.patch\n    # fix segfault on import qgis.core on OSX (link extension modules\n    # against Python::Module, not Python::Python / libpython)\n    - 0007-link-python-module.patch  # [osx]\n    # let bld.bat point sip-build at Library/bin/qmake6.exe, the qmake that\n    # has a working qt6.conf on Windows\n    - 0010-allow-qmake-executable-override.patch  # [win]\n    # build.sh uses -DQGIS_MAC_BUNDLE=FALSE; the .icns install needs the\n    # bundle's APP_RESOURCES_DIR, so skip it without a bundle\n    - 0011-mac-icons-only-in-bundle.patch  # [osx]\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  # pyproj no longer supports py311\n  skip: true  # [py2k or py<312]\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n    - m2-flex  # [win]\n    - m2-bison  # [win]\n    - m2-m4  # [win]\n    - {{ compiler('c') }}\n    - {{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - sip                                # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - pyqt-builder                       # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - pyqt6-sip                          # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - pyqt6                              # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - qscintilla2                        # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - pkgconfig                          # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - flex                               # [unix and (build_platform != target_platform)]\n    - bison                              # [unix and (build_platform != target_platform)]\n    - m4                                 # [unix and (build_platform != target_platform)]\n    - libpdal                            # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - libprotobuf                        # [build_platform != target_platform]\n  host:\n    - setuptools\n    - sip\n    - python                             # [build_platform == target_platform]\n    - six\n    - flex                               # [unix]\n    - bison                              # [unix]\n    - m4                                 # [unix]\n    - pkgconfig\n    - expat\n    - icu\n    - libzip\n    - libprotobuf\n    - libtasn1                           # [osx]\n    - exiv2\n    # Qt stack.\n    - qt6-main\n    - pyqt6                              # [build_platform == target_platform]\n    - pyqt6-sip                          # [build_platform == target_platform]\n    - pyqt-builder                       # [build_platform == target_platform]\n    # qt6-webengine isn't published for osx-64 (Intel); qt-webengine-feedstock\n    # cross-compiles it from osx-arm64 and Chromium can't cross-compile that way.\n    # https://github.com/conda-forge/qt-webengine-feedstock/pull/98\n    - qt6-webengine                      # [not (osx and x86_64)]\n    - qt6-serialport\n    - qt6-multimedia\n    - qt6-positioning\n    - qt6-3d\n    - qscintilla2\n    - qca-qt6\n    - qwt\n    - qtkeychain-qt6\n    # GDAL stack.\n    - libgdal\n    - gdal\n    - geos\n    - proj\n    # GSL for georeferencer.\n    - gsl\n    - sqlite\n    - libspatialindex 2.0\n    - libspatialite\n    # For PostgreSQL support.\n    - postgresql\n    - psycopg2\n    # Point Clouds. Need only C/C++ package\n    - libpdal\n    # no laz-perf: QGIS builds its own copy (WITH_INTERNAL_LAZPERF, default\n    # on), which needs internal headers the conda package doesn't ship, and\n    # the conda headers clash with it on Windows' include order\n    - libopencl-devel\n    - clhpp\n    - libgl-devel                            # [linux]\n    - libegl-devel                           # [linux]\n    - libopengl-devel                        # [linux]\n    - xorg-xorgproto                         # [linux]\n    - xcb-util                               # [linux]\n    - xcb-util-wm                            # [linux]\n    - xcb-util-keysyms                       # [linux]\n    - xcb-util-image                         # [linux]\n    - xcb-util-renderutil                    # [linux]\n    - xorg-libx11                            # [linux]\n    - xorg-libxext                           # [linux]\n    - xorg-libxdamage                        # [linux]\n    - xorg-libsm                             # [linux]\n    - xorg-libice                            # [linux]\n    - xorg-libxcomposite                     # [linux]\n    - xorg-libxxf86vm                        # [linux]\n    - xorg-xf86vidmodeproto                  # [linux]\n  run:\n    - python\n    - icu\n    - libzip\n    - libtasn1                               # [osx]\n    - qt6-main\n    - pyqt6\n    - pyqt6-sip\n    # qt6-webengine isn't published for osx-64 (Intel); qt-webengine-feedstock\n    # cross-compiles it from osx-arm64 and Chromium can't cross-compile that way.\n    # https://github.com/conda-forge/qt-webengine-feedstock/pull/98\n    - qt6-webengine                      # [not (osx and x86_64)]\n    - qt6-serialport\n    - qt6-multimedia\n    - qt6-positioning\n    - qt6-3d\n    - qscintilla2\n    - qca-qt6\n    - qwt\n    - qtkeychain-qt6\n    - libgdal\n    - gdal\n    - geos\n    - proj\n    - gsl\n    - sqlite\n    - libspatialindex 2.0\n    - libspatialite\n    - psycopg2\n    - postgresql\n    - exiv2\n    - libprotobuf\n    # Runtime Python library deps\n    - python-dateutil\n    - future\n    - httplib2\n    - jinja2\n    - markupsafe\n    - mock\n    - nose2\n    - plotly\n    - pygments\n    - pyproj\n    - requests\n    - six\n    - pytz\n    - pyyaml\n    - yaml\n    - owslib\n    - libpdal\n    - ocl-icd                                # [linux]\n    - khronos-opencl-icd-loader              # [win or osx]\n\ntest:\n  files:\n    - test_data\n    - test_py_qgis.py\n  commands:\n    - {{ RECIPE_DIR }}/run_test.bat          # [win]\n    - bash {{ RECIPE_DIR }}/run_test.sh      # [not win]\n\nabout:\n  home: http://qgis.org/\n  license: GPL-2.0-only\n  license_file: COPYING\n  summary: A free and open source Geographic Information System (GIS).\n  description: |\n    QGIS is a user friendly Open Source Geographic Information System (GIS)\n    licensed under the GNU General Public License. QGIS is an official\n    project of the Open Source Geospatial Foundation (OSGeo). It runs on\n    Linux, Unix, Mac OSX, Windows and Android and supports numerous vector,\n    raster, and database formats and functionalities.\n  doc_url: https://www.qgis.org/en/docs/index.html\n  dev_url: https://github.com/qgis/QGIS\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - ceholden\n    - ocefpaf\n    - kmuehlbauer\n    - SrNetoChan\n    - gillins\n    - izahn\n",
